      <h1>How to Read a <em>Resistor</em> Color Code</h1>
      <p class="dek">Those colored stripes are a standardized code for a resistor's value and precision. Read them in the right direction and four or five bands turn into an exact resistance in ohms. Here is the color-to-number system, how to tell which end to start from, and the one thing the bands never tell you.</p>
