          <li><span class="dot">1</span><div><b>Decodes and reverses.</b> Bands to value for 4, 5, and 6-band and SMD codes, or a target value back to its bands and nearest E-series match.</div></li>
          <li><span class="dot">2</span><div><b>Sizes the circuit too.</b> An Ohm's Law solver and an LED resistor calculator with current and wattage warnings, plus Arduino and Raspberry Pi presets.</div></li>
          <li><span class="dot">3</span><div><b>Readable for everyone.</b> A colorblind text mode picks band colors from labeled dropdowns rather than relying on color vision.</div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="cav">The key</div>
      <h2 id="code">What does each color mean?</h2>
      <p>Every color maps to a digit, and the same palette doubles as the multiplier. Black is 0 through white at 9 for the significant figures, the multiplier band multiplies by a power of ten, and the tolerance band gives the precision. The whole system is set by IEC 60062, and the standard resistance values themselves come from the E-series in IEC 60063 (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_color_code" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Electronic color code, per IEC 60062</a>).</p>
