        <li>Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E_series_of_preferred_numbers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">E series of preferred numbers</a> (IEC 60063 preferred values, E12 / E24 / E96).</li>
        <li>Electronics Tutorials, <a href="https://www.electronics-tutorials.ws/resistor/res_2.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resistor Colour Code</a> (read from the tolerance band end, left to right).</li>
        <li>SparkFun, <a href="https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/resistors/decoding-resistor-markings" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Decoding Resistor Markings</a> (worked 4.7 k&Omega; reverse example, tolerance band separation).</li>
        <li>Electronics Tutorials, <a href="https://www.electronics-tutorials.ws/resistor/res_7.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resistor Power Rating</a> (wattage is set by physical size, not the bands).</li>
        <li>ComponentsInfo, <a href="https://www.componentsinfo.com/1k-ohm-resistor-color-code/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">1k Ohm Resistor Color Code</a> (brown-black-red-gold worked example).</li>
      </ul>
